=\"container\">\n   262→        <div class=\"page-title\">\n   263→            <h1>Agentic Coding Research Report</h1>\n   264→        </div>\n   265→\n   266→        <main class=\"three-column-layout\">\n   267→            <section class=\"new-products\">\n   268→                <div class=\"section-header\">\n   269→                    <h2>New Products</h2>\n   270→                </div>\n   271→                <div class=\"section-content\">\n   272→                    <div class=\"empty-state\">\n   273→                        No new products detected in this period.\n   274→                    </div>\n   275→                </div>\n   276→            </section>\n   277→\n   278→            <section class=\"whitelist-updates\">\n   279→                <div class=\"section-header\">\n   280→                    <h2>Whitelist Updates</h2>\n   281→                </div>\n   282→                <div class=\"section-content\">\n   283→                    <div class=\"item\">\n   284→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n   285→                            <span class=\"update-badge feature\">Feature</span>\n   286→                            <a href=\"https://cursor.com/changelog\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Cursor - Model Controls, Spend Management, and Usage Analytics</a>\n   287→                        </div>\n   288→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   289→                            May 4, 2026 release introduces model controls for enterprise users, spend management tools, and usage analytics dashboard targeting Enterprise admins.\n   290→                        </div>\n   291→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   292→                            <span class=\"meta-source\">cursor.com</span>\n   293→                            <span class=\"meta-date\">2026-05-04</span>\n   294→                        </div>\n   295→                    </div>\n   296→\n   297→                    <div class=\"item\">\n   298→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n   299→                            <span class=\"update-badge feature\">Feature</span>\n   300→                            <a href=\"https://blakecrosley.com/blog/code-with-claude-sf-2026-recap\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Claude Code - Rate Limits Doubled for Pro, Max, Team, and Enterprise Plans</a>\n   301→                        </div>\n   302→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   303→                            On May 6, 2026, Claude Code five-hour rate limits were doubled for Pro, Max, Team, and seat-based Enterprise plans, with peak-hours throttling also addressed.\n   304→                        </div>\n   305→                        <div class=\"community-quote\">\n   306→                            \"Anthropic announced doubling of 5-hour rate limits for Pro, Max, Team, and Enterprise plans, removal of peak hours limits\"\n   307→                        </div>\n   308→                        <div class=\"community-quote\">\n   309→                            \"Users discussing hitting 20% of weekly limits in just 2 hours before the increase\"\n   310→                        </div>\n   311→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   312→                            <span class=\"meta-source\">blakecrosley.com</span>\n   313→                            <span class=\"meta-date\">2026-05-06</span>\n   314→                        </div>\n   315→                    </div>\n   316→\n   317→                    <div class=\"item\">\n   318→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n   319→                            <span class=\"update-badge bugfix\">Bugfix</span>\n   320→                            <a href=\"https://cursor.com/cn/changelog\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Cursor - Version 3.3 Bug Fixes</a>\n   321→                        </div>\n   322→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   323→                            May 6, 2026 update (v3.3) fixed various cloud agent timing and hydration edge cases affecting reliability, plus performance improvements.\n   324→                        </div>\n   325→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   326→                            <span class=\"meta-source\">cursor.com</span>\n   327→                            <span class=\"meta-date\">2026-05-06</span>\n   328→                        </div>\n   329→                    </div>\n   330→\n   331→                    <div class=\"item\">\n   332→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n   333→                            <span class=\"update-badge announcement\">Announcement</span>\n   334→                            <a href=\"https://github.blog/changelog/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">GitHub Copilot - Copilot Code Review Billing Changes (Effective June 1, 2026)</a>\n   335→                        </div>\n   336→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   337→                            GitHub announced changes to Copilot code review billing where each review will be billed as AI usage and start consuming GitHub Actions minutes.\n   338→                        </div>\n   339→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   340→                            <span class=\"meta-source\">github.blog</span>\n   341→                            <span class=\"meta-date\">2026-05-15</span>\n   342→                        </div>\n   343→                    </div>\n   344→\n   345→                    <div class=\"item\">\n   346→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n   347→                            <span class=\"update-badge release\">Release</span>\n   348→                            <a href=\"https://geminicli.com/docs/changelogs/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Gemini CLI - Version 0.41.0 with Real-Time Voice Mode</a>\n   349→                        </div>\n   350→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   351→                            Release v0.41.0 adds real-time voice mode support, secure .env loading with workspace trust in headless mode, and stronger shell command capabilities.\n   352→                        </div>\n   353→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   354→                            <span class=\"meta-source\">geminicli.com</span>\n   355→                            <span class=\"meta-date\">2026-05-15</span>\n   356→                        </div>\n   357→                    </div>\n   358→\n   359→                    <div class=\"item\">\n   360→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n   361→                            <span class=\"update-badge feature\">Feature</span>\n   362→                            <a href=\"https://github.blog/changelog/2026-04-30-github-copilot-in-visual-studio-april-update/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">GitHub Copilot - Agentic Workflows in Visual Studio</a>\n   363→                        </div>\n   364→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   365→                            April 30, 2026 update focuses on agentic workflows with cloud agent sessions launching directly from IDE and enhanced custom agent capabilities.\n   366→                        </div>\n   367→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   368→                            <span class=\"meta-source\">github.blog</span>\n   369→                            <span class=\"meta-date\">2026-04-30</span>\n   370→                        </div>\n   371→                    </div>\n   372→                </div>\n   373→            </section>\n   374→\n   375→            <section class=\"technical-insights\">\n   376→                <div class=\"section-header\">\n   377→                    <h2>Technical Insights</h2>\n   378→                </div>\n   379→                <div class=\"section-content\">\n   380→                    <div class=\"item\">\n   381→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n   382→                            <a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=40485021\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Local AI Needs to Be the Norm</a>\n   383→                        </div>\n   384→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   385→                            A Hacker News discussion (438 points) on the importance of running AI models locally. Emphasizes privacy, data sovereignty, and reducing dependence on cloud services.\n   386→                        </div>\n   387→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   388→                            <span class=\"meta-source\">Hacker News</span>\n   389→                            <span class=\"meta-tag\">local-ai</span>\n   390→                            <span class=\"meta-tag\">privacy</span>\n   391→                            <span class=\"meta-date\">2026-05-11</span>\n   392→                        </div>\n   393→                    </div>\n   394→\n   395→                    <div class=\"item\">\n   396→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n   397→                            <a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=40484512\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Task Paralysis and AI</a>\n   398→                        </div>\n   399→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   400→                            A popular Hacker News thread (185 points) discussing how AI tools affect productivity and task management, with developers sharing personal experiences.\n   401→                        </div>\n   402→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   403→                            <span class=\"meta-source\">Hacker News</span>\n   404→                            <span class=\"meta-tag\">ai-productivity</span>\n   405→                            <span class=\"meta-date\">2026-05-11</span>\n   406→                        </div>\n   407→                    </div>\n   408→\n   409→                    <div class=\"item\">\n   410→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n   411→                            <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2605.06651\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">AI Co-Mathematician: Accelerating Mathematicians with Agentic AI</a>\n   412→                        </div>\n   413→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   414→                            Paper describing an AI system designed to collaborate with mathematicians, assisting with proof generation, conjecture formation, and literature review.\n   415→                        </div>\n   416→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   417→                            <span class=\"meta-source\">arXiv</span>\n   418→                            <span class=\"meta-tag\">ai-research</span>\n   419→                            <span class=\"meta-tag\">mathematics</span>\n   420→                            <span class=\"meta-date\">2026-05-08</span>\n   421→                        </div>\n   422→                    </div>\n   423→\n   424→                    <div class=\"item\">\n   425→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n   426→                            <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2605.06365\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">From Agent Loops to Deterministic Graphs: Execution Lineage</a>\n   427→                        </div>\n   428→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   429→                            Paper addressing reproducibility challenges in AI-native workflows, proposing deterministic graphs for better tracking and reproduction of AI-assisted work.\n   430→                        </div>\n   431→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   432→                            <span class=\"meta-source\">arXiv</span>\n   433→                            <span class=\"meta-tag\">reproducibility</span>\n   434→                            <span class=\"meta-tag\">ai-agents</span>\n   435→                            <span class=\"meta-date\">2026-05-08</span>\n   436→                        </div>\n   437→                    </div>\n   438→\n   439→                    <div class=\"item\">\n   440→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n   441→                            <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2605.06614\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">SkillOS: Learning Skill Curation for Self-Evolving Agents</a>\n   442→                        </div>\n   443→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   444→                            ICML 2026 paper introducing a system for curating and evolving skills in AI agents, enabling dynamic learning and continuous improvement.\n   445→                        </div>\n   446→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   447→                            <span class=\"meta-source\">arXiv</span>\n   448→                            <span class=\"meta-tag\">skill-learning</span>\n   449→                            <span class=\"meta-tag\">icml-2026</span>\n   450→                            <span class=\"meta-date\">2026-05-08</span>\n   451→                        </div>\n   452→                    </div>\n   453→\n   454→                    <div class=\"item\">\n   455→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n   456→                            <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2605.06457\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Beyond Task Success: Measuring Workflow Fidelity in LLM-Based Agentic Payment Systems</a>\n   457→                        </div>\n   458→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   459→                            Paper discussing evaluation metrics for AI agents beyond task completion, arguing for measuring 'workflow fidelity' in high-stakes applications.\n   460→                        </div>\n   461→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   462→                            <span class=\"meta-source\">arXiv</span>\n   463→                            <span class=\"meta-tag\">evaluation</span>\n   464→                            <span class=\"meta-tag\">fintech</span>\n   465→                            <span class=\"meta-date\">2026-05-08</span>\n   466→                        </div>\n   467→                    </div>\n   468→\n   469→                    <div class=\"item\">\n   470→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n   471→                            <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2605.06390\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Automated Alignment is Harder Than You Think</a>\n   472→                        </div>\n   473→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   474→                            Paper examining challenges in automating AI alignment, demonstrating fundamental difficulties in creating systems that reliably align AI behavior with human values.\n   475→                        </div>\n   476→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   477→                            <span class=\"meta-source\">arXiv</span>\n   478→                            <span class=\"meta-tag\">ai-safety</span>\n   479→                            <span class=\"meta-tag\">alignment</span>\n   480→                            <span class=\"meta-date\">2026-05-08</span>\n   481→                        </div>\n   482→                    </div>\n   483→\n   484→                    <div class=\"item\">\n   485→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n   486→                            <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=96jN2OCOfLs\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Karpathy on 'From Vibe Coding to Agentic Engineering' at AI Ascent 2026</a>\n   487→                        </div>\n   488→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   489→                            Andrej Karpathy discussed the shift from one-shot prompt coding toward agentic engineering workflows, covering code agents and the 'Loopy Era of AI.'\n   490→                        </div>\n   491→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   492→                            <span class=\"meta-source\">YouTube</span>\n   493→                            <span class=\"meta-tag\">vibe-coding</span>\n   494→                            <span class=\"meta-tag\">agentic-engineering</span>\n   495→                            <span class=\"meta-date\">2026-05-07</span>\n   496→                        </div>\n   497→                    </div>\n   498→\n   499→                    <div class=\"item\">\n   500→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n   501→                            <a href=\"https://daringfireball.net/linked/2026/05/05/y-combinator-openai-stake\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Y Combinator's Stake in OpenAI Revealed</a>\n   502→                        </div>\n   503→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   504→                            John Gruber revealed that Y Combinator owns approximately 0.6% of OpenAI, worth over $5 billion at OpenAI's current $852 billion valuation.\n   505→                        </div>\n   506→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   507→                            <span class=\"meta-source\">Daring Fireball</span>\n   508→                            <span class=\"meta-tag\">openai</span>\n   509→                            <span class=\"meta-tag\">investment</span>\n   510→                            <span class=\"meta-date\">2026-05-05</span>\n   511→                        </div>\n   512→                    </div>\n   513→\n   514→                    <div class=\"item\">\n   515→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n   516→                            <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/May/4/granite-pelican/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Granite 4.1 LLMs Released by IBM with Apache 2.0 License</a>\n   517→                        </div>\n   518→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   519→                            IBM released Granite 4.1 family (3B, 8B, 30B) under Apache 2.0 license. Simon tested 21 quantized variants with mixed results on SVG generation tasks.\n   520→                        </div>\n   521→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   522→                            <span class=\"meta-source\">Simon Willison</span>\n   523→                            <span class=\"meta-tag\">llms</span>\n   524→                            <span class=\"meta-tag\">ibm</span>\n   525→                            <span class=\"meta-date\">2026-05-04</span>\n   526→                        </div>\n   527→                    </div>\n   528→\n   529→                    <div class=\"item\">\n   530→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n   531→                            <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/May/4/redis-arrays/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Redis Arrays Feature Built with AI Assistance</a>\n   532→                        </div>\n   533→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   534→                            Salvatore Sanfilippo submitted a PR adding array data type to Redis. Simon used Claude Code to build an interactive playground for testing these commands.\n   535→                        </div>\n   536→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   537→                            <span class=\"meta-source\">Simon Willison</span>\n   538→                            <span class=\"meta-tag\">redis</span>\n   539→                            <span class=\"meta-tag\">claude-code</span>\n   540→                            <span class=\"meta-date\">2026-05-04</span>\n   541→                        </div>\n   542→                    </div>\n   543→\n   544→                    <div class=\"item\">\n   545→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n   546→                            <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/May/2/sightings/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">iNaturalist Sightings Feature Built Entirely on Phone with Claude Code</a>\n   547→                        </div>\n   548→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   549→                            Simon built a new 'Sightings' feature for his blog using Claude Code on his phone while camping, displaying wildlife photos with filters and search.\n   550→                        </div>\n   551→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   552→                            <span class=\"meta-source\">Simon Willison</span>\n   553→                            <span class=\"meta-tag\">ai-assisted-programming</span>\n   554→                            <span class=\"meta-tag\">claude-code</span>\n   555→                            <span class=\"meta-date\">2026-05-02</span>\n   556→                        </div>\n   557→                    </div>\n   558→\n   559→                    <div class=\"item\">\n   560→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n   561→                            <a href=\"https://developer.baidu.com/article/detail.html?id=5597538\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">AI Code Generation Adoption Exceeds 85% in 2026</a>\n   562→                        </div>\n   563→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   564→                            Reports indicate AI code generation adoption has exceeded 85% in 2026, with market shifting from simple code completion to full-process automation.\n   565→                        </div>\n   566→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   567→                            <span class=\"meta-source\">TechMedia</span>\n   568→                            <span class=\"meta-tag\">ai-coding</span>\n   569→                            <span class=\"meta-tag\">adoption</span>\n   570→                            <span class=\"meta-date\">2026-05-01</span>\n   571→                        </div>\n   572→                    </div>\n   573→\n   574→                    <div class=\"item\">\n   575→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n   576→                            <a href=\"https://www.51cto.com/article/838572.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">2026 AI Programming Tools Competitive Landscape Shifting</a>\n   577→                        </div>\n   578→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   579→                            The AI programming tools market is led by Cursor, GitHub Copilot, and Windsurf, with four major categories: terminal-native agents, IDE extensions, AI-native IDEs, and orchestration platforms.\n   580→                        </div>\n   581→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   582→                            <span class=\"meta-source\">51CTO</span>\n   583→                            <span class=\"meta-tag\">ai-coding</span>\n   584→                            <span class=\"meta-tag\">market-analysis</span>\n   585→                            <span class=\"meta-date\">2026-05-01</span>\n   586→                        </div>\n   587→                    </div>\n   588→                </div>\n   589→            </section>\n   590→        </main>\n   591→\n   592→        <footer>\n   593→            <p>\n   594→                <a href=\"#\">AgentDaily</a> - Agentic Coding Research Report | Generated: 2026-05-11\n   595→            </p>\n   596→            <p style=\"margin-top: 8px;\">\n   597→                Tracking the evolution of AI-powered development tools\n   598→            </p>\n   599→        </footer>\n   600→    </div>\n   601→</body>\n   602→</html>\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"
